course: dictionary
lesson: 15200
title: Selected: chosen, or only some
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Selected is the past form of the verb select. To select something means to choose it, often with care. «Mia was selected for the school choir.» Mia was picked out from the group, so selected means chosen.
explain: Selected can also describe things that are only some, not all. «The shop has selected toys on sale.» Not every toy is cheap, only a few are. Ask yourself: is this one picked out from the rest?
explain: On a computer, selected text is marked, often in a different colour, so you can copy it or delete it. «Click and drag to select the words.» Here select means to mark. The meaning still comes from choosing: you pick the words out.
fact: Selected is the past form of the verb select: select, selects, selected, selecting.
fact: «Selected» means chosen from a group, often carefully.
fact: «Selected» can also mean only some, not all, as in «selected shops».
fact: In maths, «a number is selected at random» means it is picked by chance.
fact: Useful phrases: selected for, carefully selected, selected at random, in selected stores.
exercise: «The shop has selected toys on sale.» What does selected mean here? | Toys for dogs | *Only some toys, not all | Broken toys | Every toy in the shop
exercise: A number is selected at random from a hat. What does at random mean? | *By chance, with no plan | In the right order | Using a calculator | Very quickly
exercise: On a computer, you select a word and it turns a different colour. What does selected mean here? | *Marked so you can use it | Hidden from view | Spelled wrong | Deleted for ever
test: Which phrase means picked out carefully? | Half price | Quickly dropped | Carefully lost | *Carefully selected
test: «Only selected shops sell the game.» What does selected mean here? | Shops that are open all day | Shops that are closed | Every shop in town | *Only some shops, not all
exam: Which sentence uses selected to mean chosen from a group? | *«Ava was selected to play the lead in the play.» | «The bus selected a red colour.» | «The rain selected the path.» | «The cat is selected to be tired.»
